From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:06:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_tonemap_opencl: reshape Dolby Vision profile 5 in
 the kernel

A Dolby Vision profile 5 base layer is IPT-PQ-C2, not BT.2020 YCbCr.
tonemap_opencl took it as BT.2020 and produced wrong colours, and the
only way around it was vf_dovi_reshape on the CPU before hwupload.

With tonemap=bt2408_hable and a full range IPT-C2 input, build the
kernel with DOVI_RESHAPE: it applies the RPU polynomial and MMR
reshape and the IPT to RGB matrices per pixel from a constant buffer
filled by ff_dovi_reshape_init(), and interpolates chroma from the
frame's chroma location. The per-pixel math follows libplacebo
v7.360.1 (LGPL-2.1-or-later). Other curves, limited range input and a
frame without DOVI metadata are refused.

Against vf_dovi_reshape followed by tonemap_opencl, the direct chain
differs by a mean CIEDE2000 of 0.40 (p99 1.57) on four frames of a
1280x720 profile 5 clip. HDR10 output of all three curves at both
ranges is bit-identical to before. init and filter_frame are split
into helpers; neither grows.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
